WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.450
- I know. I know.

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:05.310
I am so honored you're here.

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:06.630
I'm such a big fan of your work.

00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:08.070
I was a fan of you before Babylon.

00:00:08.070 --> 00:00:09.930
We're going to get to it.

00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:12.150
- First of all likewise.

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:13.560
You are an icon.

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:15.387
You're iconic, Kelly.

00:00:15.387 --> 00:00:16.571
- [Kelly] Oh, you're very nice but-

00:00:16.571 --> 00:00:17.404
(crowd cheering)

00:00:17.404 --> 00:00:20.580
Y'all are going to be blown
the hell away with this movie.

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:21.988
- [Margot] Oh yeah.

00:00:21.988 --> 00:00:22.950
- The movie, your character,
I'm going to get to it.

00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:24.660
- If you thought you
just had New Year's Eve,

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:26.170
it's like you're going to
relive that vibe all over again.

00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:28.720
- It's like New Year's Eve on LSD

00:00:29.790 --> 00:00:30.900
but it's also like-

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:31.733
Okay, I'm going to get to it.

00:00:31.733 --> 00:00:32.760
I want to start with you first

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:33.840
because I do want to
talk about your project

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:34.740
but you're more important.

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:36.300
So what are you going to do this year?

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:38.610
I don't like making resolutions

00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:39.660
because I always fail at them.

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:42.210
So we're doing like, what are
you going to do better at?

00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:43.830
What are you doing for yourself this year?

00:00:43.830 --> 00:00:47.190
- I always make a ridiculous
list of resolutions,

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:49.620
most of which are totally unobtainable,

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:52.291
and then it gets to, yeah, like December

00:00:52.291 --> 00:00:53.730
and I'm like, oh, didn't do any of that.

00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:55.050
But some are achievable.

00:00:55.050 --> 00:00:57.720
Like one year I was like,
I want to learn to make jam

00:00:57.720 --> 00:01:00.450
and I was able to accomplish that.

00:01:00.450 --> 00:01:01.350
- I made jam.

00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:02.183
- [Margot] I made jam.

00:01:02.183 --> 00:01:03.120
- Was it good, jam?

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:04.290
- It was pretty good.

00:01:04.290 --> 00:01:06.600
To be honest, I'd still buy
it instead of making it,

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:07.433
but anyway.

00:01:07.433 --> 00:01:08.266
- [Kelly] It's a process.

00:01:08.266 --> 00:01:09.320
- Yeah.

00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:10.153
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:10.153 --> 00:01:10.986
- Yeah, I did it on a really hot day too,

00:01:10.986 --> 00:01:11.819
which I don't recommend.

00:01:11.819 --> 00:01:12.752
Do it in winter.

00:01:12.752 --> 00:01:14.940
Anyways, this year was
on my list last year.

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:15.780
I didn't get around to it,

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:17.817
but I really want to learn the banjo.

00:01:17.817 --> 00:01:19.550
(banjo playing)

00:01:19.550 --> 00:01:20.383
- Oh.

00:01:20.383 --> 00:01:21.540
- [Margot] Oh, my gosh.

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:23.430
I'm telling you, literally my band,

00:01:23.430 --> 00:01:24.900
they all play like everything,

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:26.670
specifically Jocko as well.

00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:28.080
- [Jocko] I am ready.

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:28.913
- You play banjo as well?

00:01:28.913 --> 00:01:29.746
You're incredible.

00:01:29.746 --> 00:01:30.579
(banjo music)

00:01:30.579 --> 00:01:33.030
Oh my gosh.

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:34.200
- [Jocko] When do we start?

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:35.850
- Oh, honestly, tomorrow.

00:01:35.850 --> 00:01:37.980
Anytime please.

00:01:37.980 --> 00:01:38.813
I'm not kidding.

00:01:38.813 --> 00:01:39.840
I've been looking for a banjo teacher.

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:41.108
- We heard!

00:01:41.108 --> 00:01:42.097
We heard you were looking
for a banjo teacher.

00:01:42.097 --> 00:01:42.930
- [Jocko] I got you.

00:01:42.930 --> 00:01:43.763
- [Kelly} We're like,
we know a banjo player.

00:01:43.763 --> 00:01:45.000
And he's really good.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:46.050
But why a banjo?

00:01:46.050 --> 00:01:47.400
I'm just curious.

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:48.233
- I don't know.

00:01:48.233 --> 00:01:50.010
It just seems like a great instrument.

00:01:50.010 --> 00:01:50.843
I love the sound of it.

00:01:50.843 --> 00:01:52.620
And I also, I know this is silly,

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:54.450
but like I think it'd be
really funny if I was ever

00:01:54.450 --> 00:01:55.290
on a camping trip

00:01:55.290 --> 00:01:57.630
and I played like the
music from Deliverance

00:01:57.630 --> 00:01:58.860
just to freak people out,

00:01:58.860 --> 00:02:00.630
like hide in a tree and do it but-

00:02:00.630 --> 00:02:01.620
- I think what would freak them out

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:03.210
if he yelled squeal, piggy, squeal.

00:02:03.210 --> 00:02:04.200
- [Margot] Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:05.033
Well I thought, look,

00:02:05.033 --> 00:02:06.090
if they don't get that reference,

00:02:06.090 --> 00:02:07.680
then there's a few go-to lines

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:10.277
and hopefully they'll pick up
on what I am doing but yeah.

00:02:10.277 --> 00:02:11.239
- Oh, my God. The banjo
is a cool instrument.

00:02:11.239 --> 00:02:13.140
- I've been learning French,

00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:15.090
but I want to be fluent in French.

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:15.930
That would be cool.

00:02:15.930 --> 00:02:19.910
- Oh, I've been learning
Spanish for decades. (laughs)

00:02:19.910 --> 00:02:22.320
Unless you practice it every day,

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:23.962
like my brain just doesn't work like that.

00:02:23.962 --> 00:02:25.380
It does not sink it.

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:27.920
I can read it, but speaking,
that's the hardest thing.

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:29.189
Do you find?

00:02:29.189 --> 00:02:31.920
- Yes, especially like
with French, it's like,

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:33.120
I'm pretty good at reading it,

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:34.440
and then if I'm hearing it,

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:36.725
and then as soon as someone
asks me to speak, I'm like,

00:02:36.725 --> 00:02:37.558
(stammers).

00:02:37.558 --> 00:02:38.391
- [Kelly] Yeah and then you tense up

00:02:38.391 --> 00:02:39.690
and you're like, I've
never heard this language

00:02:39.690 --> 00:02:40.830
in my entire life before.

00:02:40.830 --> 00:02:41.663
Yup.

00:02:41.663 --> 00:02:42.510
- On the flip side, I just work,

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:46.050
my amazing co-star, Diego
Calva, who's in Babylon.

00:02:46.050 --> 00:02:46.883
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:46.883 --> 00:02:47.910
- English is his second language.

00:02:47.910 --> 00:02:49.050
Spanish is his first language.

00:02:49.050 --> 00:02:50.370
He's from Mexico City.

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:53.100
And somehow have done this
entire journey with him

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:54.630
and still don't know,

00:02:54.630 --> 00:02:56.790
like my Spanish has not improved at all.

00:02:56.790 --> 00:02:59.220
He, meanwhile, like learnt
his English perfectly,

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:01.140
could improvise entire scenes in English.

00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:02.970
I mean he was remarkable.

00:03:02.970 --> 00:03:05.580
- It is remarkable how people
can pick it up so quickly.

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:06.413
- [Margot] Yeah.

00:03:06.413 --> 00:03:07.246
- I think it's a beautiful thing.

00:03:07.246 --> 00:03:08.790
- So many people are
bilingual, trilingual,

00:03:08.790 --> 00:03:09.623
and I'm like-

00:03:09.623 --> 00:03:10.680
- [Kelly] Yeah, especially in Europe.

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:13.620
- I only speak Australian
English, American.

00:03:13.620 --> 00:03:15.640
- I love that you said Australian.

00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:16.860
- Yeah. It's different!

00:03:16.860 --> 00:03:17.730
- Totally!

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:20.151
- It's a different lingo, you know,

00:03:20.151 --> 00:03:21.184
it's a lot to learn.

00:03:21.184 --> 00:03:22.017
- [Kelly] I love Australia.

00:03:22.017 --> 00:03:22.850
That was my first place whenever,

00:03:22.850 --> 00:03:24.300
after I went idol like 20 years ago,

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:25.770
it was the first place I like went.

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:27.030
I had no idea what rugby was.

00:03:27.030 --> 00:03:29.460
They had me performing this big
thing there and it was huge.

00:03:29.460 --> 00:03:31.050
Just like y'alls Super Bowl, I guess.

00:03:31.050 --> 00:03:31.883
And I-

00:03:31.883 --> 00:03:32.940
- It wasn't State of Origin, was it?

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:34.740
- I don't know what is it the NRL?

00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:35.640
The National Rugby League?

00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:36.724
- [Margot] Yeah.

00:03:36.724 --> 00:03:37.557
- It was this big thing.

00:03:37.557 --> 00:03:38.390
- Oh, you played for
the big, like the thing?

00:03:38.390 --> 00:03:39.223
- [Kelly] It was enormous.

00:03:39.223 --> 00:03:40.230
I had no idea what I was signing up for.

00:03:40.230 --> 00:03:41.940
And, but what I love about Australians

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:42.990
y'all are like Texans.

00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:43.823
I'm from Texas.

00:03:43.823 --> 00:03:44.850
Everybody's so nice.

00:03:44.850 --> 00:03:46.080
Like friendly, like,

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:47.010
sure, come on in!

00:03:47.010 --> 00:03:48.450
Like, everybody's just very friendly.

00:03:48.450 --> 00:03:49.283
I love Australia.

00:03:49.283 --> 00:03:51.030
- I always said, I was like,
if I was born in America

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:53.430
I'd definitely be from like
Texas or I'd be from the South.

00:03:53.430 --> 00:03:55.401
Like, that's just like
the vibe of where I'm from

00:03:55.401 --> 00:03:56.393
in Australia.

00:03:56.393 --> 00:03:57.444
- Well, especially if you
like making jam in the heat,

00:03:57.444 --> 00:03:58.890
that's very southern.

00:03:58.890 --> 00:04:00.930
- And learning the banjo.

00:04:00.930 --> 00:04:02.940
- It's all becoming clear now.

00:04:02.940 --> 00:04:05.160
Was it hard to adjust
coming from Australia?

00:04:05.160 --> 00:04:06.210
Like to America?

00:04:06.210 --> 00:04:07.043
Like, was that weird?

00:04:07.043 --> 00:04:07.980
Especially Hollywood?

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:09.960
- It was a bigger, you know,

00:04:09.960 --> 00:04:12.810
jump culturally than I was expecting.

00:04:12.810 --> 00:04:13.643
More than anything,

00:04:13.643 --> 00:04:15.810
I was just amazed to see
how many things I'd seen

00:04:15.810 --> 00:04:17.880
in the movies were actually true.

00:04:17.880 --> 00:04:19.590
I, you know, so many instances.

00:04:19.590 --> 00:04:20.423
I was like, wow,

00:04:20.423 --> 00:04:21.990
everyone does drink out
of red cups at a party

00:04:21.990 --> 00:04:23.077
and like,

00:04:23.077 --> 00:04:26.820
oh there are yellow cabs and
people do yell on the street.

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:28.710
Like it's so like, I was like, oh my God.

00:04:28.710 --> 00:04:29.670
It's just like the movies.

00:04:29.670 --> 00:04:30.503
- Do you miss being there?

00:04:30.503 --> 00:04:31.410
- [Margot] I do, all the time.

00:04:31.410 --> 00:04:32.708
- Yeah.

00:04:32.708 --> 00:04:33.541
- Yeah.

00:04:33.541 --> 00:04:34.374
- It's beautiful.

00:04:34.374 --> 00:04:35.207
- Yeah, I'm going soon but yeah.

00:04:35.207 --> 00:04:36.040
- It's wonderful.

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:36.873
It's just kind of one of the
last wild places to me too.

00:04:36.873 --> 00:04:39.030
Like I've literally done shows
out in the middle of nowhere

00:04:39.030 --> 00:04:40.740
and I was like, we all were like,

00:04:40.740 --> 00:04:44.490
so if the world ends and we're
here, who can build a fire?

00:04:44.490 --> 00:04:47.190
Like we were in the middle
of nowhere at some festival

00:04:47.190 --> 00:04:48.174
and I-

00:04:48.174 --> 00:04:49.007
- Oh yeah.

00:04:49.007 --> 00:04:49.840
- [Kelly] Bring your banjo.

00:04:49.840 --> 00:04:50.673
- [Margot] Yeah.

00:04:50.673 --> 00:04:51.506
- It was like, I didn't know
if we were going to make it.

00:04:51.506 --> 00:04:52.339
It was literally,

00:04:52.339 --> 00:04:53.396
I'd never been that kind
of place in Australia.

00:04:53.396 --> 00:04:54.300
I've been like Melbourne and Sydney

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:55.410
and all the major like cities.

00:04:55.410 --> 00:04:57.690
- But yeah, you go somewhere
like Tasmania and it's like-

00:04:57.690 --> 00:04:59.412
- [Kelly] Wildly different. Yeah.

00:04:59.412 --> 00:05:00.245
- It's wild.

00:05:00.245 --> 00:05:02.130
It's like being middle earth
like in Lord of the Rings.

00:05:02.130 --> 00:05:03.060
You're like, everything looks different.

00:05:03.060 --> 00:05:04.140
- It's kind of interesting though.

00:05:04.140 --> 00:05:05.670
It's kind of uncharted territory too,

00:05:05.670 --> 00:05:07.823
so it's kind of, it's
beautiful in that sense.

00:05:07.823 --> 00:05:08.656
- [Margot] It's so beautiful.

00:05:08.656 --> 00:05:09.489
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:05:09.489 --> 00:05:10.654
- And then New Zealand
is also like, you know,

00:05:10.654 --> 00:05:11.940
if there was ever a zombie apocalypse,

00:05:11.940 --> 00:05:13.950
like just go straight to New Zealand that-

00:05:13.950 --> 00:05:14.783
- It's so pretty.

00:05:14.783 --> 00:05:17.943
- It's beautiful but small
and like, it's just, again,

00:05:19.033 --> 00:05:20.910
they, well, they did shoot
Lord of the Rings there,

00:05:20.910 --> 00:05:21.743
so it makes sense.

00:05:21.743 --> 00:05:23.370
It's very middle earth
vibes there as well.

00:05:23.370 --> 00:05:25.284
- [Kelly] They knew what they were doing.

00:05:25.284 --> 00:05:26.117
- Yeah.

00:05:26.117 --> 00:05:26.950
- I cannot say this enough.

00:05:26.950 --> 00:05:27.783
It's incredible.

00:05:27.783 --> 00:05:28.616
You have to see it.

00:05:28.616 --> 00:05:30.870
It's incredible. It's insanity.

00:05:30.870 --> 00:05:33.210
There's chaos but then
there's like beautiful moments

00:05:33.210 --> 00:05:35.790
and it's such a trip.

00:05:35.790 --> 00:05:37.200
The whole movie is such a trip

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:39.090
but tell everybody what it's about

00:05:39.090 --> 00:05:40.980
because I don't want to
spoiler alert anything.

00:05:40.980 --> 00:05:42.180
- No! You set that up beautifully.

00:05:42.180 --> 00:05:43.013
Thank you.

00:05:43.013 --> 00:05:43.846
I love that you loved it.

00:05:43.846 --> 00:05:44.860
- It's so great.

00:05:44.860 --> 00:05:45.693
- It's so good.

00:05:45.693 --> 00:05:46.526
- [Kelly] It's wild.

00:05:46.526 --> 00:05:48.240
- It's like, the second
I read it, I was like,

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:49.980
I have to be a part of this.

00:05:49.980 --> 00:05:51.240
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:53.430
- This character's like once
in a lifetime character.

00:05:53.430 --> 00:05:55.920
This movie's like a once
in a career opportunity

00:05:55.920 --> 00:05:58.860
and you know, I get a real kick
out of when it comes around

00:05:58.860 --> 00:06:01.320
to like Halloween time and
seeing like what, you know,

00:06:01.320 --> 00:06:03.210
18 year olds are dressing
up for as Halloween.

00:06:03.210 --> 00:06:04.800
Like there's a lot of
Harley Quinn's for sure,

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:08.070
but there's like a resurgence
with the younger generation

00:06:08.070 --> 00:06:09.812
with Wolf of Wall Street.

00:06:09.812 --> 00:06:10.680
We made that 10 years ago.

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:11.738
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:06:11.738 --> 00:06:12.780
- For some reason like 18
year olds are dressing up

00:06:12.780 --> 00:06:15.123
as Naomi and Jordan and I was like, wow.

00:06:15.123 --> 00:06:15.956
- It's because of all the streaming.

00:06:15.956 --> 00:06:16.789
All these people are, they don't know.

00:06:16.789 --> 00:06:17.928
- They're like, finding it again.

00:06:17.928 --> 00:06:18.761
- Yeah.

00:06:18.761 --> 00:06:19.594
- And or like Scarface, it's like,

00:06:19.594 --> 00:06:21.780
that's a huge Halloween
costume for young people.

00:06:21.780 --> 00:06:23.160
And I'm like, that's amazing

00:06:23.160 --> 00:06:25.290
that people are going back
and still loving, you know.

00:06:25.290 --> 00:06:26.123
So I really care about-

00:06:26.123 --> 00:06:27.227
- You're right though.

00:06:27.227 --> 00:06:28.060
This is one of those films.

00:06:28.060 --> 00:06:28.893
- I think so.

00:06:28.893 --> 00:06:29.726
- Yeah.

00:06:29.726 --> 00:06:30.559
- Like I want to be a part of films

00:06:30.559 --> 00:06:31.410
that people are going
to watch for decades.

00:06:31.410 --> 00:06:32.460
- It's thought-provoking.

00:06:32.460 --> 00:06:33.293
- Yeah.

00:06:33.293 --> 00:06:34.197
- I literally stopped watching it

00:06:34.197 --> 00:06:35.910
and I called my manager
my friends and my friends

00:06:35.910 --> 00:06:38.760
and I was like, I don't even
know what to say, right.

00:06:38.760 --> 00:06:40.680
Like, and we had this
whole conversation about-

00:06:40.680 --> 00:06:42.360
Because I also think that
when you see the movie

00:06:42.360 --> 00:06:44.220
you'll get something different from it.

00:06:44.220 --> 00:06:46.890
Because I know that the
movie is obviously about

00:06:46.890 --> 00:06:47.760
going the, you know,

00:06:47.760 --> 00:06:50.310
the progression of film
going from silent film-

00:06:50.310 --> 00:06:51.143
- To talkies.

00:06:51.143 --> 00:06:51.976
- Yes.

00:06:51.976 --> 00:06:53.550
- So I know that that's the main theme.

00:06:53.550 --> 00:06:55.950
But there's also about how this town

00:06:55.950 --> 00:06:58.320
it can be beautiful and
wonderful and so much awe

00:06:58.320 --> 00:07:01.470
but like, it can also exploit
its own and eat its own.

00:07:01.470 --> 00:07:02.303
And it's like-

00:07:02.303 --> 00:07:03.522
- Totally.

00:07:03.522 --> 00:07:04.355
- It's all that's there.

00:07:04.355 --> 00:07:06.807
- It's kind of like a real,
like, people keep saying like,

00:07:06.807 --> 00:07:07.751
oh it's a love,

00:07:07.751 --> 00:07:09.180
Damien's writing a love
letter to Hollywood.

00:07:09.180 --> 00:07:12.032
And I was like, I think
it's true but it's kinda-

00:07:12.032 --> 00:07:13.399
- [Kelly] It's a really
messed up letter. (laughs)

00:07:13.399 --> 00:07:14.232
- It's kind of like,

00:07:14.232 --> 00:07:15.960
it's almost like it's real true love

00:07:15.960 --> 00:07:18.120
because Damian, our
director, is not shying away

00:07:18.120 --> 00:07:20.957
from the really ugly parts
of Hollywood as well.

00:07:20.957 --> 00:07:21.790
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:07:21.790 --> 00:07:22.623
- You know, back then

00:07:22.623 --> 00:07:23.456
but also it is majorly a reflection

00:07:23.456 --> 00:07:24.289
of where we're at now too.

00:07:24.289 --> 00:07:26.160
But you know, it's like wow,

00:07:26.160 --> 00:07:27.150
he really loves it

00:07:27.150 --> 00:07:30.450
because he can see all the
really gross, awful sides

00:07:30.450 --> 00:07:32.250
of it too and the magical sides of it.

00:07:32.250 --> 00:07:33.870
And then he's giving you all of that

00:07:33.870 --> 00:07:36.990
in this like epic, entertaining,

00:07:36.990 --> 00:07:39.600
like, it's a masterpiece.

00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:42.000
But it's, I mean, it's so funny as well.

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:43.650
Like it's-

00:07:43.650 --> 00:07:44.520
- [Kelly] Your character-

00:07:44.520 --> 00:07:45.353
- [Margot] It's laugh out loud hilarious.

00:07:45.353 --> 00:07:46.186
- [Kelly] It is funny.

00:07:46.186 --> 00:07:48.240
But your character, like, I'm not kidding,

00:07:48.240 --> 00:07:49.898
her character is Nelly-

00:07:49.898 --> 00:07:50.731
(Margot laughing)

00:07:50.731 --> 00:07:52.953
You should win every award

00:07:52.953 --> 00:07:54.900
because I feel like you
played every possible role

00:07:54.900 --> 00:07:56.040
you could have played in this film

00:07:56.040 --> 00:07:57.840
because there's drugs involved.

00:07:57.840 --> 00:08:00.690
So there's like, there's
like the mania kind of side,

00:08:00.690 --> 00:08:03.270
there's the emotional
side, the dreamer side,

00:08:03.270 --> 00:08:06.660
the hurt side, like when the family passed

00:08:06.660 --> 00:08:08.520
and like the single tear thing,

00:08:08.520 --> 00:08:10.470
the silent with a single tear thing.

00:08:10.470 --> 00:08:13.290
It's so funny how they
kept having you repeat it.

00:08:13.290 --> 00:08:15.150
I heard that one day or two days

00:08:15.150 --> 00:08:17.520
you danced like 14 hours
straight, like two days in a row.

00:08:17.520 --> 00:08:19.145
- Oh no, that was like two weeks.

00:08:19.145 --> 00:08:19.978
- Like what happened to your body?

00:08:19.978 --> 00:08:20.811
- It was like-

00:08:20.811 --> 00:08:21.644
- [Kelly] What happened?

00:08:21.644 --> 00:08:22.477
How do you do that?

00:08:22.477 --> 00:08:23.310
- I don't know.

00:08:23.310 --> 00:08:24.143
- Because this is not normal dancing.

00:08:24.143 --> 00:08:25.162
Are they talking about
the scene at the party?

00:08:25.162 --> 00:08:26.217
- [Margot] Yeah. Yeah.

00:08:26.217 --> 00:08:27.182
- Holy!

00:08:27.182 --> 00:08:29.490
- Yeah, that was, I
mean, yeah, that was it.

00:08:29.490 --> 00:08:30.690
If you see it, you'll be like-

00:08:30.690 --> 00:08:33.000
- How did you not break
something in those heels?

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:35.250
Or your, did you do yoga every day?

00:08:35.250 --> 00:08:37.414
Like how did you, like I'm to,

00:08:37.414 --> 00:08:38.640
this dance scene is incredible.

00:08:38.640 --> 00:08:40.590
- I mean that whole sequence was so mad.

00:08:40.590 --> 00:08:44.070
We were in that room with all
those people for two weeks,

00:08:44.070 --> 00:08:46.650
I reckon and I mean it
was like being at a party

00:08:46.650 --> 00:08:47.483
that never ended.

00:08:47.483 --> 00:08:48.450
It was like being like a bender

00:08:48.450 --> 00:08:49.800
that you couldn't get out of.

00:08:49.800 --> 00:08:51.120
But it was so-

00:08:51.120 --> 00:08:52.350
- Which is kind of the
point of that party.

00:08:52.350 --> 00:08:53.614
That's what it is.

00:08:53.614 --> 00:08:54.447
- Which is what you meant to feel like.

00:08:54.447 --> 00:08:55.538
Yeah. Yeah.

00:08:55.538 --> 00:08:57.540
- And, but yeah, I do this
whole big crazy dance sequence

00:08:57.540 --> 00:08:59.910
and it was just like wild and fun.

00:08:59.910 --> 00:09:02.760
But like, I had like all the
background artists around me

00:09:02.760 --> 00:09:04.680
a lot of them were actual
professional dancers.

00:09:04.680 --> 00:09:06.400
A lot of them, you know,
were just, you know,

00:09:06.400 --> 00:09:07.560
other background artists.

00:09:07.560 --> 00:09:09.540
Some were just friends of
like Damien and Olivia's.

00:09:09.540 --> 00:09:12.360
Like, it was just a real
great group of people

00:09:12.360 --> 00:09:13.950
and everyone would just
hype each other up.

00:09:13.950 --> 00:09:14.783
- Oh my gosh.

00:09:14.783 --> 00:09:16.320
The scene that you had to
keep doing over and over

00:09:16.320 --> 00:09:18.930
because they were figuring
out how to do sound.

00:09:18.930 --> 00:09:21.270
And you had to keep in character

00:09:21.270 --> 00:09:22.103
and you had to keep you,

00:09:22.103 --> 00:09:24.600
and I mean, would y'all
just lose it on each other?

00:09:24.600 --> 00:09:26.152
- Oh my God.

00:09:26.152 --> 00:09:27.062
- [Kelly] That is incredible.

00:09:27.062 --> 00:09:27.895
- That escalated.

00:09:27.895 --> 00:09:29.070
That scene got so out of hand.

00:09:29.070 --> 00:09:30.150
It's so funny though.

00:09:30.150 --> 00:09:31.500
That was like one when
I read in the script

00:09:31.500 --> 00:09:33.120
and I was like crying with laughter

00:09:33.120 --> 00:09:35.490
and when you watch it, you'll
be crying with laughter but-

00:09:35.490 --> 00:09:36.627
- [Kelly] Oh my god.

00:09:36.627 --> 00:09:39.270
- Yeah, it's like, that's
why this movie is so amazing

00:09:39.270 --> 00:09:41.280
because you think of the 1920s Hollywood

00:09:41.280 --> 00:09:43.890
and I think of like Great Gatsby parties.

00:09:43.890 --> 00:09:44.730
- Think of the glamor.

00:09:44.730 --> 00:09:46.890
- You know, a champagne coupe
and like the Charleston.

00:09:46.890 --> 00:09:47.760
- [Kelly] This is behind the curtain.

00:09:47.760 --> 00:09:50.100
- This is like wow.

00:09:50.100 --> 00:09:50.933
It's like-

00:09:50.933 --> 00:09:52.068
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:09:52.068 --> 00:09:52.901
- [Margot] Mad.

00:09:52.901 --> 00:09:53.734
And it was all true.

00:09:53.734 --> 00:09:54.567
Like all these stories.

00:09:54.567 --> 00:09:55.400
- [Kelly] It even addresses
like racism and like-

00:09:55.400 --> 00:09:56.233
- [Margot] Oh yeah.

00:09:56.233 --> 00:09:57.066
- [Kelly] I mean just like,
it addresses everything.

00:09:57.066 --> 00:09:57.899
- That scene that Jovan does at the end.

00:09:57.899 --> 00:10:01.036
I mean it's so, it's gut-wrenching.

00:10:01.036 --> 00:10:01.869
- Yeah, you play Sidney.

00:10:01.869 --> 00:10:02.910
- Yep. It's play Sidney Palma.

00:10:02.910 --> 00:10:05.637
Yeah and Li Li's character is just

00:10:05.637 --> 00:10:06.780
like hugely based on Anna May Wong.

00:10:06.780 --> 00:10:07.860
- It's so incredible.

00:10:07.860 --> 00:10:09.780
So you use a movement coach,

00:10:09.780 --> 00:10:12.000
which I've also heard people use.

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:14.160
And they teach you to
be like certain animals.

00:10:14.160 --> 00:10:15.870
I've actually heard this before as well

00:10:15.870 --> 00:10:17.490
and this must be a thing.

00:10:17.490 --> 00:10:18.323
- It's a thing.

00:10:18.323 --> 00:10:19.599
- Yes.

00:10:19.599 --> 00:10:20.432
- I didn't go to so drama school,

00:10:20.432 --> 00:10:21.265
so I don't know

00:10:21.265 --> 00:10:22.590
if this is something that
everyone does in drama school

00:10:22.590 --> 00:10:24.540
but it's something I discovered after.

00:10:24.540 --> 00:10:25.860
It's something I actually started doing

00:10:25.860 --> 00:10:27.120
when I was on I, Tonya.

00:10:27.120 --> 00:10:28.320
So that was like the first time-

00:10:28.320 --> 00:10:30.000
- What was your animal for I, Tonya?

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:31.200
- I was a pit bull.

00:10:31.200 --> 00:10:32.033
- [Kelly] A pit bull?

00:10:32.033 --> 00:10:33.960
- Yeah, because they're
very misunderstood.

00:10:33.960 --> 00:10:34.793
You know, like-

00:10:34.793 --> 00:10:35.961
- [Kelly] I like a pit bull.

00:10:35.961 --> 00:10:36.794
- At first glance you're kind of like,

00:10:36.794 --> 00:10:38.160
oh, should I be scared?

00:10:38.160 --> 00:10:40.160
I have a pit bull too,
so I love pit bulls.

00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:41.048
- Oh, I like pit bulls.

00:10:41.048 --> 00:10:42.264
- I love a pit bull. Yeah.

00:10:42.264 --> 00:10:43.097
But yeah, I wanted like
with her ice skates on

00:10:43.097 --> 00:10:43.980
I wanted to be heavy on the feet.

00:10:43.980 --> 00:10:45.420
I wanted her to feel like,

00:10:45.420 --> 00:10:47.250
I wanted the character
to feel like the world

00:10:47.250 --> 00:10:49.770
was like just bearing
down on her all the time.

00:10:49.770 --> 00:10:52.290
But then on the ice, she's a
mustang, like a wild horse,

00:10:52.290 --> 00:10:53.460
like when she's ice skating.

00:10:53.460 --> 00:10:55.050
So she's two animals really.

00:10:55.050 --> 00:10:57.704
And then, yeah, every
character I've had animals.

00:10:57.704 --> 00:10:58.537
- [Kelly] Who is Nelly?

00:10:58.537 --> 00:10:59.574
- Nelly, this is going to sound-

00:10:59.574 --> 00:11:00.822
- There's a lot of people in there.

00:11:00.822 --> 00:11:04.980
- She's, yeah, she's an
octopus and a honey badger.

00:11:04.980 --> 00:11:07.003
- Well octopus, yeah, she's always-

00:11:07.003 --> 00:11:07.938
(crosstalk)

00:11:07.938 --> 00:11:08.771
- About to say that.

00:11:08.771 --> 00:11:09.604
- I have honey badgers on my ranch.

00:11:09.604 --> 00:11:10.437
Those are mean little-

00:11:10.437 --> 00:11:11.270
- Do you really?

00:11:11.270 --> 00:11:12.103
- Yes, they are mean.

00:11:12.103 --> 00:11:12.936
- They're insane.

00:11:12.936 --> 00:11:13.769
- Yeah.

00:11:13.769 --> 00:11:15.180
Oh, I just, you're the honey badger.

00:11:15.180 --> 00:11:16.440
The scene when you're eating all the stuff

00:11:16.440 --> 00:11:17.273
with the rich people.

00:11:17.273 --> 00:11:18.553
- Yes, that's the honey badger.

00:11:18.553 --> 00:11:19.386
- [Kelly] Yes. Yes.

00:11:19.386 --> 00:11:21.390
- And then the the snake fight scene,

00:11:21.390 --> 00:11:22.440
that's all honey badger,

00:11:22.440 --> 00:11:24.380
like because there are actual videos

00:11:24.380 --> 00:11:26.130
