00:11:26.130 --> 00:11:27.330
There's videos of honey badgers,

00:11:27.330 --> 00:11:30.482
which aren't huge animals,
fighting like lions.

00:11:30.482 --> 00:11:31.315
- [Kelly] But they're mighty

00:11:31.315 --> 00:11:33.510
- And they have like really thick skin

00:11:33.510 --> 00:11:34.343
and they're just-

00:11:34.343 --> 00:11:35.283
- [Kelly] That is Nelly.

00:11:35.283 --> 00:11:36.200
- Like, insane.

00:11:36.200 --> 00:11:37.200
Yeah. She has very thick skin.

00:11:37.200 --> 00:11:38.339
- Yeah.

00:11:38.339 --> 00:11:39.870
- Like, and she just fights anything

00:11:39.870 --> 00:11:41.790
and anyone at the drop of a hat.

00:11:41.790 --> 00:11:43.154
And playful-

00:11:43.154 --> 00:11:43.987
- I love this trick.

00:11:43.987 --> 00:11:44.820
- [Margot] Yeah.

00:11:44.820 --> 00:11:45.653
- Yeah.

00:11:45.653 --> 00:11:47.302
- It's helpful because you do
all this research and like,

00:11:47.302 --> 00:11:48.135
you know, there's tons of research

00:11:48.135 --> 00:11:49.287
and you read all these books
and watch all these films

00:11:49.287 --> 00:11:50.752
and get all these facts
about the real life people

00:11:50.752 --> 00:11:53.100
at this time and what,
you know, and sometimes

00:11:53.100 --> 00:11:55.290
your head gets so clouded with, you know,

00:11:55.290 --> 00:11:57.570
statistics and facts and
the history and bla bla bla-

00:11:57.570 --> 00:11:59.336
- Simplify just with movement, yeah.

00:11:59.336 --> 00:12:00.360
- But if you just revert
back to the animal

00:12:00.360 --> 00:12:02.760
then you can just be
